(3160521, 439826, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I think your soft focus hurt your score with this image.  Studying the capture, it looks like a glamour-type soft filter of some sort was used.  While it gives the image a appealing look, I think that it serves as more of a distraction than anything else.  Looking through your previous comments, it seems that the voters felt the same way.  <br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Overall, the lighting is fairly even and nice, but the highlight at the top of the glass is a bit distracting.  It competes too much with the viewer''s eye, thus pulling the eye away from the meat of the composition.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I really like the idea, and the sticky relation is easily made.  However, I would like to have seen this one with a longer trail of chocolate.  With short stream abruptly dropping out of the frame, you also cause the viewer''s eye to drop right out with it.  With a looser crop, you would have allowed the eye to flow more through the image rather than right out of the frame.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I believe that you did a nice job meeting the image is a very creative manner.  I think with a more crisp focus and a litter better lighting, this one would have pulled a much better score.  Even with the adjustments that could have been made, I think the 4.7 is a little low. <br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: I think your soft focus hurt your score with this image.  Studying the capture, it looks like a glamour-type soft filter of some sort was used.  While it gives the image a appealing look, I think that it serves as more of a distraction than anything else.  Looking through your previous comments, it seems that the voters felt the same way.   Lighting: Overall, the lighting is fairly even and nice, but the highlight at the top of the glass is a bit distracting.  It competes too much with the viewer''s eye, thus pulling the eye away from the meat of the composition. Composition/Content: I really like the idea, and the sticky relation is easily made.  However, I would like to have seen this one with a longer trail of chocolate.  With short stream abruptly dropping out of the frame, you also cause the viewer''s eye to drop right out with it.  With a looser crop, you would have allowed the eye to flow more through the image rather than right out of the frame. My Opinion: I believe that you did a nice job meeting the image is a very creative manner.  I think with a more crisp focus and a litter better lighting, this one would have pulled a much better score.  Even with the adjustments that could have been made, I think the 4.7 is a little low.  Eric', '2006-12-29 18:15:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3160585, 439261, 50641, '<td valign="top">I really liked this - in my world, it would have done much better.</td>', 'I really liked this - in my world, it would have done much better.', '2006-12-29 18:41:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3160606, 439850, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I''ll echo what is already here...nothing looks focused.  I do see that the label is focused, but your DOF gives the illusion that the total image is out of focus.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Too harsh with a washed out background.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> The angle of your crop is uncomfortable.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Looking through your portfolio, there are some very strong, well-executed images there.  You obviously know how the voters vote and you are very capable of producing strong images.  I am at a loss trying to understand what you were after here.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: I''ll echo what is already here...nothing looks focused.  I do see that the label is focused, but your DOF gives the illusion that the total image is out of focus. Lighting: Too harsh with a washed out background. Composition/Content: The angle of your crop is uncomfortable. My Opinion: Looking through your portfolio, there are some very strong, well-executed images there.  You obviously know how the voters vote and you are very capable of producing strong images.  I am at a loss trying to understand what you were after here. Eric', '2006-12-29 18:51:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3160647, 439008, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Nice, crisp focus and a very nice white balance that yielded terrific color.  The blue provides a very nice background that really makes your subject stand out.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I think that your lighting is what pulled this image down as far as your score goes.  There are several hot spots from the harsh flash that are fairly distracting. Your straight-on lighting also caused some harsh shadows that also pulled from the end score.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I like the content, but the composition needed better execution.  The tilt of the top candlestick gives a crowded feeling to the overall image.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Great subject and a fine job meeting the challenge.  With a little better composition and lighting, this score would have been a good deal better.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Nice, crisp focus and a very nice white balance that yielded terrific color.  The blue provides a very nice background that really makes your subject stand out. Lighting: I think that your lighting is what pulled this image down as far as your score goes.  There are several hot spots from the harsh flash that are fairly distracting. Your straight-on lighting also caused some harsh shadows that also pulled from the end score. Composition/Content: I like the content, but the composition needed better execution.  The tilt of the top candlestick gives a crowded feeling to the overall image. My Opinion: Great subject and a fine job meeting the challenge.  With a little better composition and lighting, this score would have been a good deal better. Eric', '2006-12-29 19:17:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3161173, 439871, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, welcome to DPC.  I see that you have been here just over a month.  I hope you are enjoying the challenges, as well as learning a bit here and there.  The first thing that strikes me about your image is the size.  Smaller images always get hammered by the voters.  There are some tutorials available to help with properly sizing images for the challenges.  If you use PaintSHop, check <a href="//www.konador.com/pp/files/dpcinpsp/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">HERE</a>, and if you use PhotoSHop, check <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">HERE</a>.<br/> <br/>Get this sizing issue handled, and I believe that your scores will fare much, much better.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First of all, welcome to DPC.  I see that you have been here just over a month.  I hope you are enjoying the challenges, as well as learning a bit here and there.  The first thing that strikes me about your image is the size.  Smaller images always get hammered by the voters.  There are some tutorials available to help with properly sizing images for the challenges.  If you use PaintSHop, check HERE, and if you use PhotoSHop, check HERE. Get this sizing issue handled, and I believe that your scores will fare much, much better. Eric', '2006-12-29 22:57:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3161228, 438547, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Nice focus and fine settings to keep all the necessary elements in focus.  Your chosen white balance also yields very nice tones and coloring.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I really enjoy the warmth that you created with your lighting in this capture.  The green and brown hues of the background work nicely to set your subject off.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Very creative thinking to meet the challenge.  It still seems a bit too centered to me, and the tilt of the tabletop(?), very horizon-like, gives the image an uncomfortable feel.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> You absolutely met the challenge, but I don''t think it was what the voters had in mind. Even still, with a bit different composition and a straightened horizon line, I think your score would have grown.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Nice focus and fine settings to keep all the necessary elements in focus.  Your chosen white balance also yields very nice tones and coloring. Lighting: I really enjoy the warmth that you created with your lighting in this capture.  The green and brown hues of the background work nicely to set your subject off. Composition/Content: Very creative thinking to meet the challenge.  It still seems a bit too centered to me, and the tilt of the tabletop(?), very horizon-like, gives the image an uncomfortable feel. My Opinion: You absolutely met the challenge, but I don''t think it was what the voters had in mind. Even still, with a bit different composition and a straightened horizon line, I think your score would have grown. Eric', '2006-12-29 23:24:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3161292, 438237, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, welcome to DPC!!!  I see that this is your first challenge, so I want to be the first to welcome you to the good times and the heartaches of this site.  I think you can gain a lot of valuable knowledge on this site.  Just keep shooting away and submitting your work to the praises and criticisms of others.  I think that this is the way we learn best.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Excellent focus the produces a very crisp image.  I also like your depth of field choice here.  Your white balance is also spot-on, thus yielding the exact colors that the eye expects to see.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Too harsh.  That is the downfall of this image.  I think that the overall image looks a bit washed out and is lacking some much needed contrast.  I hope you don''t mind, but I took this version of your image and made a few adjustments.  I took the highlights down in Photoshop, as well as gave it a nice s-curve adjustment layer.  This is how I would have processed it:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=444301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/36065/thumb/444301.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/36065/thumb/444301.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/36065/thumb/444301.jpg"/></a> <br/>If you''d rather your copyrighted work not be re-displayed, please let me know and I''ll be happy to take it down.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I will have to disagree with pamelasue in that I don''t think any more of the waffle is necessary.  I think the composition that you put together looks just as it should.  The fork is a bit centered, but it really works in this particular capture.  The fork works very nicely to pull the eye into the image and the waffles serve as boundaries to keep it in and flowing around.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> This is the beginning of an excellent shot.  It it were a little underexposed your score would have surely soared.  5.3 is a very respectable score, but this one had a much higher potential.  I hope this helps.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First of all, welcome to DPC!!!  I see that this is your first challenge, so I want to be the first to welcome you to the good times and the heartaches of this site.  I think you can gain a lot of valuable knowledge on this site.  Just keep shooting away and submitting your work to the praises and criticisms of others.  I think that this is the way we learn best. Camera Work/Technical: Excellent focus the produces a very crisp image.  I also like your depth of field choice here.  Your white balance is also spot-on, thus yielding the exact colors that the eye expects to see. Lighting: Too harsh.  That is the downfall of this image.  I think that the overall image looks a bit washed out and is lacking some much needed contrast.  I hope you don''t mind, but I took this version of your image and made a few adjustments.  I took the highlights down in Photoshop, as well as gave it a nice s-curve adjustment layer.  This is how I would have processed it: If you''d rather your copyrighted work not be re-displayed, please let me know and I''ll be happy to take it down. Composition/Content: I will have to disagree with pamelasue in that I don''t think any more of the waffle is necessary.  I think the composition that you put together looks just as it should.  The fork is a bit centered, but it really works in this particular capture.  The fork works very nicely to pull the eye into the image and the waffles serve as boundaries to keep it in and flowing around. My Opinion: This is the beginning of an excellent shot.  It it were a little underexposed your score would have surely soared.  5.3 is a very respectable score, but this one had a much higher potential.  I hope this helps. Eric', '2006-12-29 23:48:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3161356, 439777, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Nice capture and very nice focus.  I also see some sort of color hue as well.  I think that your post-processing is the culprit here.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Excellent use of natural lighting.  His face is lit terrifically and nothing is lost in shadows or blown highlights.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I echo the adoration of previous commenters in that the expression is priceless.  I do think that your cropping is just a bit tight.  It give the image a very crowded and cramped feeling to it.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I like it, and I think it fits the challenge nicely.  With a bit looser crop and less the hue, you score would have surely grown.  <br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Nice capture and very nice focus.  I also see some sort of color hue as well.  I think that your post-processing is the culprit here. Lighting: Excellent use of natural lighting.  His face is lit terrifically and nothing is lost in shadows or blown highlights. Composition/Content: I echo the adoration of previous commenters in that the expression is priceless.  I do think that your cropping is just a bit tight.  It give the image a very crowded and cramped feeling to it. My Opinion: I like it, and I think it fits the challenge nicely.  With a bit looser crop and less the hue, you score would have surely grown.   Eric', '2006-12-30 00:18:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3161410, 439860, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> You captured terrific colors in this image.  I also like your choice of settings, capturing all elements of interest in crisp focus.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Your lighting is nice and even.  You did a very nice job capturing this one without loosing any details in the shadows or blown highlights.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I''d like to see your cropping loosened up a bit.  Chopping off fingers or body parts near joints gives more of an accidental snapshot than an intentionally composed image.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> You met the challenge well, but with a bit different composition, this score would have finished much higher.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: You captured terrific colors in this image.  I also like your choice of settings, capturing all elements of interest in crisp focus. Lighting: Your lighting is nice and even.  You did a very nice job capturing this one without loosing any details in the shadows or blown highlights. Composition/Content: I''d like to see your cropping loosened up a bit.  Chopping off fingers or body parts near joints gives more of an accidental snapshot than an intentionally composed image. My Opinion: You met the challenge well, but with a bit different composition, this score would have finished much higher. Eric', '2006-12-30 00:42:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3161736, 439853, 21629, '<td valign="top">Personally I think the yellow honey and pink tongue makes the skin appear green and ugly. It''s a good photo nonetheless. Congratulations on the blue ribbon.</td>', 'Personally I think the yellow honey and pink tongue makes the skin appear green and ugly. It''s a good photo nonetheless. Congratulations on the blue ribbon.', '2006-12-30 06:54:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162263, 439880, 50641, '<td valign="top">DPC loves focus!  And sometimes, simplicity. Now me, I prolly woulda destroyed this by putting leetle faces on the fingers :)</td>', 'DPC loves focus!  And sometimes, simplicity. Now me, I prolly woulda destroyed this by putting leetle faces on the fingers :)', '2006-12-30 13:50:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162294, 438329, 50641, '<td valign="top">Excellent capture - love the colors!  Even if someone weren''t familiar with the PMOW - I think the fact that it looks like a blob of rainbow jelly kinda hints that it''s sticky!  I like the comp but you might have taken some hits from the knee-jerk-centered-subject-haters.  Great find - and your processing is really bringing out the wow in all your photos lately.  I''m glad because they are really wow-worthy :)</td>', 'Excellent capture - love the colors!  Even if someone weren''t familiar with the PMOW - I think the fact that it looks like a blob of rainbow jelly kinda hints that it''s sticky!  I like the comp but you might have taken some hits from the knee-jerk-centered-subject-haters.  Great find - and your processing is really bringing out the wow in all your photos lately.  I''m glad because they are really wow-worthy :)', '2006-12-30 14:09:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162538, 439771, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>The first thing that strikes me about your image is the size.  Smaller images always get hammered by the voters.  There are some tutorials available to help with properly sizing images for the challenges.  If you use PaintSHop, check <a href="//www.konador.com/pp/files/dpcinpsp/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">HERE</a>, and if you use PhotoSHop, check <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">HERE</a>.<br/> <br/>Get this sizing issue handled, and I believe that your scores will fare much, much better.  As far as the quality of the image goes, I''ll echo the opinions of other voters that offered comments.  There really is no focal point of the image, thus nothing really grabs the eye to offer any appeal.  I can tell that it is sticky, but, without the title, I really couldn''t see what it was.  Work on your focus, as well as getting those images as large as possible.<br/> <br/>Eric</td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  The first thing that strikes me about your image is the size.  Smaller images always get hammered by the voters.  There are some tutorials available to help with properly sizing images for the challenges.  If you use PaintSHop, check HERE, and if you use PhotoSHop, check HERE. Get this sizing issue handled, and I believe that your scores will fare much, much better.  As far as the quality of the image goes, I''ll echo the opinions of other voters that offered comments.  There really is no focal point of the image, thus nothing really grabs the eye to offer any appeal.  I can tell that it is sticky, but, without the title, I really couldn''t see what it was.  Work on your focus, as well as getting those images as large as possible. Eric', '2006-12-30 16:20:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162556, 439384, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, congrats on your best finish to date, as well as your third highest score.  Well-done and well-deserved.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> This looks like it was a ton of work.  You came up with a nicely creative concept and executed it nicely as well.  Your focus is crisp and clear, and your tones are near flawless.  My only complaint is that the Gaussian blur you added gave it too much of a cartoon-type feel.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Your use of HDR yielded very nice and even lighting results.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Very creative.  I really like the stickies that have fallen off onto the floor.  This added a lot of interest to the photograph, thus giving the appearance of a man falling apart under stress.  Well seen in your mind''s eye.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Definitely the best of the three similar entries.  I think that you may have pulled a bit higher of a score without the background blur, but it worked well with the voters as it is.<br/> <br/>Eric</td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First of all, congrats on your best finish to date, as well as your third highest score.  Well-done and well-deserved. Camera Work/Technical: This looks like it was a ton of work.  You came up with a nicely creative concept and executed it nicely as well.  Your focus is crisp and clear, and your tones are near flawless.  My only complaint is that the Gaussian blur you added gave it too much of a cartoon-type feel. Lighting: Your use of HDR yielded very nice and even lighting results. Composition/Content: Very creative.  I really like the stickies that have fallen off onto the floor.  This added a lot of interest to the photograph, thus giving the appearance of a man falling apart under stress.  Well seen in your mind''s eye. My Opinion: Definitely the best of the three similar entries.  I think that you may have pulled a bit higher of a score without the background blur, but it worked well with the voters as it is. Eric', '2006-12-30 16:35:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162575, 439762, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Very clean, crisp focus, as well as a great depth of field.  Also, your choice of white balance created very nice, warm tones providing a very inviting feeling to the image.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I''d really like to see more light on the side of her face that is toward the camera.  While the shadows fit nicely into this image, this part of her face is a bit too dark, thus pulling and holding the viewer''s eye into the dark void.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I agree that this one needed a tongue, but I also think some nose should have been included.  Without the nose, the faces looks like it has some sort of uncomfortable deformity.  This one was not far off the first place finisher.  I even like your tones better, but you needed that nose.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I think the concept is far batter than the score it pulled, but it suffered in its execution.  This really  wasn''t far from being a personal best.  In my opinion, it only needed a nose and a little less shadow.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Very clean, crisp focus, as well as a great depth of field.  Also, your choice of white balance created very nice, warm tones providing a very inviting feeling to the image. Lighting: I''d really like to see more light on the side of her face that is toward the camera.  While the shadows fit nicely into this image, this part of her face is a bit too dark, thus pulling and holding the viewer''s eye into the dark void. Composition/Content: I agree that this one needed a tongue, but I also think some nose should have been included.  Without the nose, the faces looks like it has some sort of uncomfortable deformity.  This one was not far off the first place finisher.  I even like your tones better, but you needed that nose. My Opinion: I think the concept is far batter than the score it pulled, but it suffered in its execution.  This really  wasn''t far from being a personal best.  In my opinion, it only needed a nose and a little less shadow. Eric', '2006-12-30 16:46:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162596, 439674, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Very nice white balance choice, yielding great colors and strong tones.  The bottom flower looks a little out of focus to me.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> The bottom flower is also just a bit overexposed.  There are also some distraction hot spots on most of the thorns.  Shooting at a different time of day might have helped this a bit.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I like the flow you created with the angle of the vine.  It serves well to pull the viewer''s eye up and into the image.  I think that the content is a bit lacking.  While I fully understand your interpretation, it was apparently not what the voters were looking for.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I think that the voters had more of a messy liquid theme in mind.  Even still, with a little sharper focus and a little less exposure, I think this capture would have finished much higher.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Very nice white balance choice, yielding great colors and strong tones.  The bottom flower looks a little out of focus to me. Lighting: The bottom flower is also just a bit overexposed.  There are also some distraction hot spots on most of the thorns.  Shooting at a different time of day might have helped this a bit. Composition/Content: I like the flow you created with the angle of the vine.  It serves well to pull the viewer''s eye up and into the image.  I think that the content is a bit lacking.  While I fully understand your interpretation, it was apparently not what the voters were looking for. My Opinion: I think that the voters had more of a messy liquid theme in mind.  Even still, with a little sharper focus and a little less exposure, I think this capture would have finished much higher. Eric', '2006-12-30 16:59:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162610, 438478, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Terrific model and wonderful color with this capture.  Everything looks very crisp, save the cotton candy on the stick.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I think the lighting accounts for the soft look the the candy has.  I think that side of the frame is just a bit hot causing the candy to blend into the background.  The large bright spot also creates a distraction that pulls the eye from the attractive model and the great expression.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Very well planned and executed.  I do agree that the glasses frame should either be up a little or down a little.  Running it straight through the eyes makes the eyes look very distorted.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I like it, and I think that it should have scored much better even as it.  Moving the glasses and toning down the left lighting would have surely boosted it as well.<br/> <br/>Eric</td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Terrific model and wonderful color with this capture.  Everything looks very crisp, save the cotton candy on the stick. Lighting: I think the lighting accounts for the soft look the the candy has.  I think that side of the frame is just a bit hot causing the candy to blend into the background.  The large bright spot also creates a distraction that pulls the eye from the attractive model and the great expression. Composition/Content: Very well planned and executed.  I do agree that the glasses frame should either be up a little or down a little.  Running it straight through the eyes makes the eyes look very distorted. My Opinion: I like it, and I think that it should have scored much better even as it.  Moving the glasses and toning down the left lighting would have surely boosted it as well. Eric', '2006-12-30 17:13:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162752, 439529, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Very clean, crisp focus!  You also captured some terrific color and a great depth of field.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Terrific use and manipulation of lighting in RAW to yield a very nice contrast between the lit subject and the dark background while not losing any of the web detail.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Also very nice.  The web provides a great flow to encourage the viewer''s eye to roam the entire frame.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Well-seen and well-captured.  This is also a very creative way to meet this challenge nicely.  Well done!<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Very clean, crisp focus!  You also captured some terrific color and a great depth of field. Lighting: Terrific use and manipulation of lighting in RAW to yield a very nice contrast between the lit subject and the dark background while not losing any of the web detail. Composition/Content: Also very nice.  The web provides a great flow to encourage the viewer''s eye to roam the entire frame. My Opinion: Well-seen and well-captured.  This is also a very creative way to meet this challenge nicely.  Well done! Eric', '2006-12-30 18:25:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162792, 439712, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Great focus and terrific post-processing.  The arm looks a little discolored and blurry, providing a mild distraction that attracts the eye.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> All of your elements are very nicely and evenly lit.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Terrific composition.  The angle of the arm provides a great line to lead the eye up and into the image, and up to the subject of the image.  I don''t personally like the uneven, black framing.  It looks more accidental than designed, but I rarely hold points for borders.  I would not have held points for this one, but it really didn''t add to the quality either.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Looking through the challenge results, this one is far better than MANY that finished ahead of it.  I think that the odd tone on the skin may have contributed to the lower than expected score, but who am I to think I have voters figured out?<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Great focus and terrific post-processing.  The arm looks a little discolored and blurry, providing a mild distraction that attracts the eye. Lighting: All of your elements are very nicely and evenly lit. Composition/Content: Terrific composition.  The angle of the arm provides a great line to lead the eye up and into the image, and up to the subject of the image.  I don''t personally like the uneven, black framing.  It looks more accidental than designed, but I rarely hold points for borders.  I would not have held points for this one, but it really didn''t add to the quality either. My Opinion: Looking through the challenge results, this one is far better than MANY that finished ahead of it.  I think that the odd tone on the skin may have contributed to the lower than expected score, but who am I to think I have voters figured out? Eric', '2006-12-30 18:48:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162850, 439476, 52467, '<td valign="top">Nice finish..cool shot!</td>', 'Nice finish..cool shot!', '2006-12-30 19:21:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162876, 439880, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I like the detail you captured here with the spot-on focus.  The fingerprint detail is very nice.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Great job with terrifically even lighting on all parts of the subject.  I do think that the background is a bit too bright for this one, giving it a somewhat washed out feeling.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> While the sticky relation is easily made, I think that you needed more sticky than just the little dot between the fingers.  Other than that, you have a strong composition that leads the eye up and down the entire image.  Very well executed.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I think this one scored a bit low.  This is a fine macro, but who am I to think I understand the voters.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: I like the detail you captured here with the spot-on focus.  The fingerprint detail is very nice. Lighting: Great job with terrifically even lighting on all parts of the subject.  I do think that the background is a bit too bright for this one, giving it a somewhat washed out feeling. Composition/Content: While the sticky relation is easily made, I think that you needed more sticky than just the little dot between the fingers.  Other than that, you have a strong composition that leads the eye up and down the entire image.  Very well executed. My Opinion: I think this one scored a bit low.  This is a fine macro, but who am I to think I understand the voters. Eric', '2006-12-30 19:28:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162893, 439746, 43298, '<td valign="top">HAHAHAHAHAA! This is hilarious :)</td>', 'HAHAHAHAHAA! This is hilarious :)', '2006-12-30 19:38:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162927, 439800, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Nice focus and a very nice job only focusing on the elements of the image.  The use of the sheet was a very nice touch to prevent any sort of distractions in the background.  I also see some sort of yellow hue to the image.  I think increasing the skin tones was unnecessary for this capture.  It look over-warmed as it is.  I''d be really interested in seeing the original.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I like the lighting you used here.  You did a good job creating highlights and shadows that give a nice depth to the image.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> While I do not usually withhold points for borders, this one is far too distracting.  You have great content for this challenge that is nicely composed.  The border is far too strong for the tones inside the frame, thus it competes strongly for the eye''s attention.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> First-rate job meeting the challenge, but I''d be willing to bet the border and the hue/sat on the skin tones kept this one out of the 6 range.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Nice focus and a very nice job only focusing on the elements of the image.  The use of the sheet was a very nice touch to prevent any sort of distractions in the background.  I also see some sort of yellow hue to the image.  I think increasing the skin tones was unnecessary for this capture.  It look over-warmed as it is.  I''d be really interested in seeing the original. Lighting: I like the lighting you used here.  You did a good job creating highlights and shadows that give a nice depth to the image. Composition/Content: While I do not usually withhold points for borders, this one is far too distracting.  You have great content for this challenge that is nicely composed.  The border is far too strong for the tones inside the frame, thus it competes strongly for the eye''s attention. My Opinion: First-rate job meeting the challenge, but I''d be willing to bet the border and the hue/sat on the skin tones kept this one out of the 6 range. Eric', '2006-12-30 19:51:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3162938, 437411, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Pretty good focus, but I''d like to see more of the center coin.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I think that the lighting is a bit harsh here and that the shadows are more of a distraction than a valuable element of the image.  While I am a fan of higher contrast images, this one is almost hard to view.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Nice work using the curve and angle of the tape to give the image flow.  The eye enters and goes either up or down the tape, stopping to study each coin.  <br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Nice composition, but I think removing the shadows, or at least toning down the contrast, would have pulled a better score.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Pretty good focus, but I''d like to see more of the center coin. Lighting: I think that the lighting is a bit harsh here and that the shadows are more of a distraction than a valuable element of the image.  While I am a fan of higher contrast images, this one is almost hard to view. Composition/Content: Nice work using the curve and angle of the tape to give the image flow.  The eye enters and goes either up or down the tape, stopping to study each coin.   My Opinion: Nice composition, but I think removing the shadows, or at least toning down the contrast, would have pulled a better score. Eric', '2006-12-30 19:57:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3163112, 438983, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> As other voters have commented, the focus needs some work.  The captured colors are very nice, but I think a color other than white would have been better for this one.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> The lighting is off.  Your background is a bit too bright and your subject a bit too dark.  Perhaps some fill flash would have benefited the end results here.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Your composition is too centered for this shot.  While I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I think a more offset subject would have also helped.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I think with a few small adjustments, this one could have pulled a better score.  I do like the creativity of meeting the challenge, as this is the only shot of its type that I remember in the results.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: As other voters have commented, the focus needs some work.  The captured colors are very nice, but I think a color other than white would have been better for this one. Lighting: The lighting is off.  Your background is a bit too bright and your subject a bit too dark.  Perhaps some fill flash would have benefited the end results here. Composition/Content: Your composition is too centered for this shot.  While I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I think a more offset subject would have also helped. My Opinion: I think with a few small adjustments, this one could have pulled a better score.  I do like the creativity of meeting the challenge, as this is the only shot of its type that I remember in the results. Eric', '2006-12-30 21:14:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3163133, 439572, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Great focus and spot on skin tones.  Your depth of field is a bit too shallow as some of the items on your face appear out of focus.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Nice, even lighting.  There are no harsh shadows or blown highlights.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I think that this one suffered from taking a common theme in the challenge.  There were quite a few entries that were very similar to this, and even more with at lease something sticking to the face.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I think that this one placed close to its potential.  Also, you do fine work with shower curtains.  This one provided a pretty good result.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Great focus and spot on skin tones.  Your depth of field is a bit too shallow as some of the items on your face appear out of focus. Lighting: Nice, even lighting.  There are no harsh shadows or blown highlights. Composition/Content: I think that this one suffered from taking a common theme in the challenge.  There were quite a few entries that were very similar to this, and even more with at lease something sticking to the face. My Opinion: I think that this one placed close to its potential.  Also, you do fine work with shower curtains.  This one provided a pretty good result. Eric', '2006-12-30 21:26:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3163156, 439441, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I like the choice you made with the depth of field, but I think that the focus should have been reversed.  I feel that she should have been crisp in the foreground and he soft in the background as she is the ''speaking'' subject in the image.  I do like the black and white conversion you accomplished.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> She''s a little overexposed, and his jacket causes some deep dark areas that are lacking detail.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Strong composition, and this would be a fine entry for some other challenge.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I''d have to agree with the voters that have commented earlier in that it is a stretch to make this one meet the challenge.  Voters are very, very harsh, as you can tell, when they feel that the entry doesn''t meet the challenge.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: I like the choice you made with the depth of field, but I think that the focus should have been reversed.  I feel that she should have been crisp in the foreground and he soft in the background as she is the ''speaking'' subject in the image.  I do like the black and white conversion you accomplished. Lighting: She''s a little overexposed, and his jacket causes some deep dark areas that are lacking detail. Composition/Content: Strong composition, and this would be a fine entry for some other challenge. My Opinion: I''d have to agree with the voters that have commented earlier in that it is a stretch to make this one meet the challenge.  Voters are very, very harsh, as you can tell, when they feel that the entry doesn''t meet the challenge. Eric', '2006-12-30 21:32:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3163233, 439731, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I like your choice of settings that yielded every element in crisp focus, as well as the tones and colors that you captured.  I also like the long exposure that you used to make the Christmas lights flare into stars.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Also very nice.  Your use of the Christmas lights provides a very warm, inviting feel to the image.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Also very strong, in my opinion.  I really like how the window sill draws the eye into the image and the boots, Christmas lights and city lights hold it and keep it moving.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I think you really stretched this one to meet the challenge, as did most of the voters.  When I''m going through voting, I rarely look at the image titles.  Rather, I rely on the content of the frame to meet the challenge.  I have been hammered on this at times myself, so I fully understand.  I think that it is a strong image, but it just doesn''t fit into the challenge.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: I like your choice of settings that yielded every element in crisp focus, as well as the tones and colors that you captured.  I also like the long exposure that you used to make the Christmas lights flare into stars. Lighting: Also very nice.  Your use of the Christmas lights provides a very warm, inviting feel to the image. Composition/Content: Also very strong, in my opinion.  I really like how the window sill draws the eye into the image and the boots, Christmas lights and city lights hold it and keep it moving. My Opinion: I think you really stretched this one to meet the challenge, as did most of the voters.  When I''m going through voting, I rarely look at the image titles.  Rather, I rely on the content of the frame to meet the challenge.  I have been hammered on this at times myself, so I fully understand.  I think that it is a strong image, but it just doesn''t fit into the challenge. Eric', '2006-12-30 22:02:39.000000', NULL, 0),
